    "description": "CoolCo provides district cooling services to buildings in downtown Cincinnati. Its customer base includes commercial office, hotel, retail, government, institutional, and other downtown building owners that purchase chilled-water service for interior cooling and process loads. The system follows an asset-heavy utility model based on central plant and distribution infrastructure with recurring service revenues. Public materials state that CoolCo has served the Cincinnati central business district since 1997 and that the system can produce more than 10,000 tons of cooling. Harrison Street acquired the district energy system in 2019, and the current ownership split is not publicly disclosed. The business continues to operate as an urban district-cooling utility serving the Cincinnati core.",
